>so darn great, why oh why didn't I see the Gnome Lord in the room?

>Is this a bug (3.0j plevel 10, on UNIX(SUN)), or just a feature?

Well, I find the whole illumination system used in Nethack to be quite
absurd. It is "strange" that when you apply a lamp in a dark room that room
gets lit forever (a magic lamp can do it, but a lamp like the ones you buy
at the shop near to your home isn't supposed to be so effective :-).
It is "strange" that lit rooms are lit forever and you cannot see any torch
or lamp burning. To be fair this can be explained if you consider that the
dungeon is a magic place: it is possible that the wizard casted a spell on
lit rooms. Obviously using magic you can explain everything...

However, when you're in a dark room you can still see the 8 adiacent squares,
so the room is not so dark, uh? A really dark room must make you feel totally
blind.

If you want to change radically the game, you can ask (I'm asking it now!) to
the dev team to implement something like torches to be used to illuminate rooms
and corridors. However you need one hand to hold the torch, so you cannot wield
a two-handed weapon while you are wielding a light source, but you can wear
a miner-helmet with a lamp on it, or a wizard can cast some spells that
makes lit the quares around him. Note that the most important point of this
proposal is that a location can be lit only if there is a light source
that makes it lit, and that (non-magical) light sources last only a finite
amount of time.
To make a room lit for some time you can drop a torch (or a lamp) in the room.
I think that Moria uses such a system, or something close to it. This can add
something to the strategic part of the game, because you heavily depend on
light sources to win the game, probably more than on food.
Torches and lamps must be quite common (you can use a piece of wood as a torch,
if you have matches to ignite it!) and you must find them in shops in fair
number to keep the game not too difficult. Telepaty can also be extended to
work not only when you are blind but even if you are in the dark and you
cannot see nothing (much like wearing a blindfold). In this case telepaty
can be limited to a small radius around the character, like when using an
helm of telepaty.


Ok, that's all. I know that this proposal is a quite radical, but I enjoy
to think ways to make Nethack more challenging. I'd like to hear comments,
on the news, not by mail!
